@@ -123,10 +123,36 @@
 
 Text of a custom banner message. The default banner is "tcllib smtpd 1.6".
 Note that changing the banner does not affect the bracketing text
 in the full greeting, printing status 220, server-address, and timestamp.
 
+[def "[option -usetls] [arg boolean]"]
+
+If true and the [package tls] package is available, the server offers
+the [const STARTTLS] extension (RFC 3207) to its clients. A client
+issuing [const STARTTLS] switches the session to TLS, using the TLS
+options described below. If the [package tls] package cannot be loaded
+the option is silently ignored. The default is [const false].
+
+[def "[option -cadir] [arg dir]"]
+[def "[option -cafile] [arg file]"]
+[def "[option -certfile] [arg file]"]
+[def "[option -cipher] [arg string]"]
+[def "[option -command] [arg cmd]"]
+[def "[option -keyfile] [arg file]"]
+[def "[option -password] [arg cmd]"]
+[def "[option -request] [arg boolean]"]
+[def "[option -require] [arg boolean]"]
+[def "[option -ssl2] [arg boolean]"]
+[def "[option -ssl3] [arg boolean]"]
+[def "[option -tls1] [arg boolean]"]
+
+These options are passed unchanged to [cmd tls::import] when a client
+issues [const STARTTLS]. See the documentation of the [package tls]
+package for their meaning. A server certificate and key (options
+[option -certfile] and [option -keyfile]) are normally required.
+
 [def "[option -validate_host] [arg proc]"]
 
 Callback to authenticate new connections based on the ip-address of
 the client.
 

